## Universal Sorting

### Define What 'Comparable' Means

```xiom
interface Comparable {
  fn is_greater(&self, other: &Self) -> Bool;
  fn is_equal(&self, other: &Self) -> Bool;
}
```

If a type can answer 'am I greater than that?' and 'are we equal?', it's sortable.

### Implement for Int Wrapper

```xiom
type Score { value: Int; }
fn Score.is_greater(&self, other: &Score) -> Bool { self.value > other.value }
fn Score.is_equal(&self, other: &Score) -> Bool { self.value == other.value }
```

### A Sorting Function

```xiom
fn sort[T: Comparable](items: &mut Vec[T]) {
  let mut i = 0;
  while i < items.len() {
    let mut j = i + 1;
    while j < items.len() {
      if items.get(i).unwrap().is_greater(items.get(j).unwrap()) {
        let temp = items.get(i).unwrap().clone();
        items.set(i, items.get(j).unwrap().clone());
        items.set(j, temp);
      }
      j += 1;
    }
    i += 1;
  }
}
```

This is bubble sort. One function sorts Scores, Names, Dates, or anything Comparable.

